 Mexican food grocery products produced and marketed in North America. It was originally the name of an American chain of Mexican restaurants that was founded in 1975 by Marno McDermott and former Green Bay Packers player Max McGee. The owners sold the rights to use the brand's name on packaged grocery products beginning in 1987. The name was also used by a former European franchise through 2024 when its last location closed in Austria."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-chi-chi-s"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chi-Chi's"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Mexican cuisine","cuisine/mexican-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Mexico in My Kitchen","ref":"site/mexicoinmykitchen-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"mexicoinmykitchen.com","note":"Mely Martínez's long-running blog of Mexican home-style recipes.","url":"https://www.mexicoinmykitchen.com/","suggested":true,"kind":"blog"},{"name":"Pati Jinich","ref":"site/patijinich-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"patijinich.com","note":"Recipe archive from the Mexican-born chef and host of the PBS series Pati's Mexican Table.","url":"https://patijinich.com/recipes/","suggested":true,"kind":"site"}]},{"h":"More from Mexican cuisine","links":[["Acapulco Mexican Restaurant and Cantina","dish/acapulco-mexican-restaurant-and-cantina"],["Amigos (restaurant chain)","dish/amigos-restaurant-chain"],["Animalón","dish/animalon"],["Anna's Taqueria","dish/anna-s-taqueria"],["Baker's Drive-Thru","dish/baker-s-drive-thru"],["Barburrito","dish/barburrito"],["Birrieria La Plaza","dish/birrieria-la-plaza"],["Birrieria PDX","dish/birrieria-pdx"],["Boca Grande Taqueria","dish/boca-grande-taqueria"],["BurritoVille","dish/burritoville"],["Cafe Rio","dish/cafe-rio"],["California Tortilla","dish/california-tortilla"],["Cantina Mariachi","dish/cantina-mariachi"],["Carlos'n Charlie's","dish/carlos-n-charlie-s"],["Casa Bonita","dish/casa-bonita"],["Casa Enrique","dish/casa-enrique"],["Casa Vega","dish/casa-vega"],["Chevys Fresh Mex","dish/chevys-fresh-mex"],["Chico's Tacos","dish/chico-s-tacos"],["Chile con queso","dish/chile-con-queso"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"],["Chimichanga","dish/chimichanga"],["Chiquito (restaurant)","dish/chiquito-restaurant"],["Concha","dish/concha"],["Contramar","dish/contramar"],["Cosecha","dish/cosecha"],["Del Taco","dish/del-taco"],["Discada","dish/discada"],["District Taco","dish/district-taco"],["Don Pablo's","dish/don-pablo-s"],["El Adobe de Capistrano","dish/el-adobe-de-capistrano"],["El Bajío (restaurant)","dish/el-bajio-restaurant"],["El Chico (restaurant)","dish/el-chico-restaurant"],["El Coyote Cafe","dish/el-coyote-cafe"],["El Fenix (restaurant)","dish/el-fenix-restaurant"],["El Gallo Taqueria","dish/el-gallo-taqueria"],["El Tepeyac Café","dish/el-tepeyac-cafe"],["El Torito","dish/el-torito"],["Em (restaurant)","dish/em-restaurant"],["Esquina Común","dish/esquina-comun"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/d/de/Former_Chi-Chi%27s_restaurant_in_Alexandria%2C_Virginia.png","w":500,"h":444,"by":"Nostaljack at English Wikipedia","lic":"Public domain","licUrl":"","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Former_Chi-Chi's_restaurant_in_Alexandria%2C_Virginia.png"}},"ingredient/lettuce":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/lettuce","n":"Lettuce","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 5 dishes across 3 cuisines","intro":[["Lettuce (Lactuca sativa) is an annual plant of the family Asteraceae mostly grown as a leaf vegetable. The leaves are most often used raw in green salads, although lettuce is also seen in other kinds of food, such as sandwiches, wraps and soups; it can also be grilled. Its stem and seeds are sometimes used; celtuce (asparagus lettuce) is one variety grown for its stems, which are eaten either raw or cooked. In addition to its main use as a leafy green, it has also gathered religious and medicinal significance over centuries of human consumption. Europe and North America originally dominated the market for lettuce, but by the late 20th century the consumption of lettuce had spread throughout the world. In 2023, world production of lettuce (and chicory) was 28 million tonnes, led by China with 53% of the total."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-lettuce"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lettuce"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":3,"groups":[["American cuisine","cuisine/american-cuisine",[["Club sandwich","dish/club-sandwich"],["Hamburger","dish/hamburger"],["Jibarito","dish/jibarito"]]],["Indonesian cuisine","cuisine/indonesian-cuisine",[["Selat solo","dish/selat-solo"]]],["Vietnamese cuisine","cuisine/vietnamese-cuisine",[["Shaking beef","dish/shaking-beef"]]]]},{"h":"Where it's grown","grown":{"what":"Lettuce and chicory","years":"2020 to 2024","url":"https://www.fao.org/faostat/en/#data/QCL","world":28147240,"top":[["China","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",14720002],["United States of America","cuisine/american-cuisine",4362848],["India","cuisine/indian-cuisine",1172266],["Spain","cuisine/spanish-cuisine",957046],["Italy","cuisine/italian-cuisine",685302],["Turkey","cuisine/turkish-cuisine",560666],["Japan","cuisine/japanese-cuisine",553075],["Belgium","cuisine/belgian-cuisine",547764],["Mexico","cuisine/mexican-cuisine",537214],["Niger","cuisine/cuisine-of-niger",483003],["France","cuisine/french-cuisine",451888],["Iran","cuisine/iranian-cuisine",435534],["Netherlands","cuisine/dutch-cuisine",248388],["Germany","cuisine/german-cuisine",225074],["Ashmore and Cartier Is.","cuisine/australian-cuisine",140454]]}},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Mayonnaise","ingredient/mayonnaise"],["Tomato","ingredient/tomato"],["Cheese","ingredient/cheese"],["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Soy sauce","ingredient/soy-sauce"],["Bacon","ingredient/bacon"],["Chicken","ingredient/chicken"],["Toast","ingredient/toast"],["Turkey as food","ing